Sunita took me to a large machine.
That espresso machine seemed very intimidating.
I had never used such a machine before.
But I was eager to learn to operate it.
Sunita showed me the different parts of the machine.
"Maya, look here," she said.
"This first dial is for water," Sunita explained.
"And this second dial is for steam."
I listened to all her instructions carefully.
Then she showed me the milk steam wand.
"This wand gets very hot," Sunita said.
"Therefore, it must be used very carefully."
I gave my full attention to that machine.
I was learning to use those dials and wand safely.
Sunita was standing next to me.
She had explained everything to me very well.
I felt a little scared at first.
But now I was ready to make my first coffee.
